# .NET version pins

When changing the target framework or SDK, update every pin in the same change:

1. `src/Directory.Build.props` and any csproj that hardcodes `<TargetFramework>`
2. Plugin `Notes.txt` samples that show a TFM
3. `global.json` SDK version (`allowPrerelease: true` only for prerelease SDKs)
4. `.github/workflows/dotnet.yml` `dotnet-version`
5. `Dockerfile` `mcr.microsoft.com/dotnet/sdk` and `aspnet` tags
6. Matching `Microsoft.AspNetCore.*`, `Microsoft.Extensions.*`, `Microsoft.Data.Sqlite`, and `System.Configuration.ConfigurationManager` package versions

```xml
<!-- ❌ BAD: TFM bumped, packages still on the previous major -->
<TargetFramework>net11.0</TargetFramework>
<PackageReference Include="Microsoft.AspNetCore.Mvc.NewtonsoftJson" Version="10.0.12" />

<!-- ✅ GOOD: TFM and framework packages on the same train -->
<TargetFramework>net11.0</TargetFramework>
<PackageReference Include="Microsoft.AspNetCore.Mvc.NewtonsoftJson" Version="11.0.0-rc.3.26522.148" />
```

Do not rewrite unrelated versions (npm lockfiles, third-party NuGet majors). For a full upgrade workflow, follow `.cursor/skills/upgrade-dotnet/SKILL.md`.
